<title>UK: Maintenance pushes UK August oil output to '96 low.</title>
<headline>Maintenance pushes UK August oil output to '96 low.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A heavy schedule of routine maintenance work pushed U.K. oil production in August to the lowest monthly level in 1996, the Aberdeen Petroleum Report (APR) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The APR said U.K. North Sea crude oil and liquids production averaged 2.35 million barrels per day (bpd) in August, down from 2.51 million bpd in July.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
